{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791622046,"nonce":"yjsuzQA2SbZa2PEUvmk/WWaFFV0=","message":"Design for CSS transitions and animations (2026-10-10), decided while scoping the complete user-agent sheet.\n\nWhere: the addon (native/src/motion.rs), next to apply_paint. blinc_abi already exposes everything needed (PaintWrite, Cascade::keyframes, Stylesheet::keyframe_list/offsets/declarations), so it needs no change there. The cascade already delivers transition and animation declarations to css_restyle as var()-resolved text; they are filtered out today because they are neither layout nor paint.\n\nHow: css_restyle diverts a node's paint writes through the motion state when the node has a transition. The first style a node gets applies at once; a later change to a transitioned field starts a tween from the value shown, so an interrupted transition continues from where it is. Animations resolve @keyframes by name and write the interpolated field each tick. Start times are taken at the first tick, so a restyle needs no clock and offscreen tests are deterministic.\n\nClock: the host passes the time. Layout.tickMotion(now) applies the frame's values and reports whether anything still moves; the window painter calls it before encoding and asks for another frame while it does. Nothing runs, and no frames are requested, when nothing is animating.\n\nInterpolated: opacity, colours (premultiplied), border radius, outline width and offset, solid backgrounds and same-shape gradients, shadows, transforms (decomposed), filters. Everything else flips at the midpoint. Layout properties (width, padding...) do not animate; that is the FLIP work and stays here.\n\nExit: an element with animations running can be waited on (HostElement.animationsFinished), so a component sets [closing], waits, then removes the node.","files":null}]}